Package: vault-rs
Version: 0.0.0-replaced-by-makefile
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: replaced-by-makefile
Recommends: openssl
Maintainer: Jérôme Poulin <jeromepoulin@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/ticpu/vault-rs
Description: PKI certificate management for HashiCorp Vault
 Issues, signs, inspects, verifies and exports certificates from a Vault PKI
 mount, and forwards every verb it does not model to the vault CLI with the
 server address and token already resolved. Output is one record per line for
 grep and awk, with an exit code that distinguishes an expiring certificate
 from a failure so cron and monitoring can act on it. Certificates and keys it
 issues are cached locally under a key held in the operator's own KV mount.
 Requires the vault CLI for passthrough subcommands, and openssl for
 --text output.
